# KEUR-DOC-011 — AGENTS.md carries its agreed chapters.
# @implements ADR-061, docs/design/doc-chapter-contract.md
#
# absence engine, maturity 2: the agents.md popular-section set, pinned to agreed
# headings with a small closed alias set. The format itself requires no fields,
# so this is keur's house contract, not an upstream mandate. Code style and PR
# instructions are required from CMMI-3; this rule covers the CMMI-2 three.
id: KEUR-DOC-011
ilities: [analysability]
maturity: 2
title: AGENTS.md is missing an agreed chapter (Project overview / Setup / Build and test)
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: absence
action: warn
target:
  filenames: AGENTS.md
patterns:
  - regex: (?im)^#{1,}\s+(Project overview|Overview)\b
    message: "AGENTS.md has no Project overview chapter — accepted: Project overview (canonical), Overview. One line; link README, don't restate it."
  - regex: (?im)^#{1,}\s+(Setup|Dev environment|Development|Getting started)\b
    message: "AGENTS.md has no Setup chapter — accepted: Setup (canonical), Dev environment, Development, Getting started. Exact commands; link CONTRIBUTING as the owner."
  - regex: (?im)^#{1,}\s+(Build and test|Build & test|Build and tests|Testing|Test)\b
    message: "AGENTS.md has no Build and test chapter — accepted: Build and test (canonical), Build & test, Testing, Test. The literal gate the agent must run before finishing."
confidence: 0.5
fix: "Add the chapter with a canonical heading or agreed alias (doc-chapter-contract.md). Keep AGENTS.md terse and literal; the owner of command detail is CONTRIBUTING — link it, don't duplicate it."
